  "note": "Gold for the research planner, written from the text of each question alone (the planner never sees a source: it plans before any page is read), before the planner or the harness was run. A gold item is a thing a person reading the question would list: the names it uses, the subjects it is about, the assertions it makes or presupposes. Where a scenario is named the question is the scenario's own. 'slots' are the content words of an item, each slot with the alternative words that meet it (inflections included); an item is covered when a plan item holds enough of its slots as whole words (see thresholds.json, planTopicCoverage). 'named' marks an entity the question writes in capitals (a proper name, an acronym, a title): only those count towards the registered entity floor, because a deterministic reader can only be asked to find names; the others are labelled so that they are reported apart. A claim is an assertion a source could confirm or contradict and that the question itself makes or presupposes: never a fact that only a source would hold.",
